Using the Maximum Power Transfer Theorem, \(R_L=R_{TH}\) The Thevenin equivalent resistance seen by the load is, \(R_{TH}=100~\Omega\) The maximum power transferred to the load is \[P_{\max}
=
\frac{V_{TH}^{2}}{4R_{TH}}\] Here, \[V_{TH}=10~\text{V},
\qquad
R_{TH}=100~\Omega\] Therefore, \[P_{\max}
=
\frac{10^2}{4\times100}
=
\frac{100}{400}
=
0.25~\text{W}\] Hence, the correct answer is \[\boxed{\textbf{C. }0.25~\text{W}}\]

